<section class="section-spacing bg-muted/30">
  <div class="container max-w-4xl">
    <h1 class="heading-xl mb-6 text-center">Free Digital Analytics Health Check</h1>
    <p class="body-lg mx-auto max-w-3xl text-center text-muted-foreground">Answer a short set of questions about your current measurement setup to get a practical view of where to focus next. It is designed for teams that want a clear starting point before a deeper technical review.</p>
  </div>
</section>
<section class="section-spacing"><div class="container grid max-w-5xl gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2">
  <div><h2 class="heading-md mb-5">What the Health Check evaluates</h2><p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">The assessment asks about GA4 and GTM, website or mobile-app measurement, conversion and ad-platform setup, confidence in reporting, missing events, consent setup, server-side/CAPI maturity, ownership, and implementation priorities. Its recommendations are grouped around reliability, coverage, attribution, privacy, and ownership.</p></div>
  <div><h2 class="heading-md mb-5">Who it is for</h2><p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">Use it when your team needs a structured conversation about measurement before deciding whether an audit, implementation, or reporting project is appropriate. It is useful for website owners, ecommerce teams, and agencies working through an inherited or evolving analytics setup.</p></div>
</div></section>
<section class="section-spacing bg-muted/30"><div class="container max-w-5xl"><h2 class="heading-md mb-8 text-center">How the assessment works</h2><ol class="grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-3"><li class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-background p-6"><strong class="text-primary">1. Describe the setup</strong><p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">Answer concise questions about the systems and gaps you know about.</p></li><li class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-background p-6"><strong class="text-primary">2. Get a score</strong><p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">Your answers are used to produce a high-level maturity score and priority themes.</p></li><li class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-background p-6"><strong class="text-primary">3. Choose a next step</strong><p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">Use the recommendations to decide whether to investigate, implement, or request expert help.</p></li></ol></div></section>
<section class="section-spacing"><div class="container max-w-5xl grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2"><div><h2 class="heading-md mb-5">What the score means</h2><p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">The score is a self-reported planning signal, not a certification or a complete technical assessment. It helps frame the areas that may deserve attention, but implementation priorities still depend on the systems, access, and business context behind your answers.</p></div><div><h2 class="heading-md mb-5">Privacy and limitations</h2><p class="leading-7 text-muted-foreground">The tool does not crawl your website, inspect source code, scan analytics requests, or audit a GTM container. It assesses the answers you provide. A technical Tracking Audit is the appropriate next step when you need implementation evidence or a prioritised remediation plan.</p></div></div></section>
<section class="section-spacing bg-muted/30"><div class="container max-w-4xl"><h2 class="heading-md mb-8">Common questions</h2><div class="space-y-4"><details class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-background p-5"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold">Is this a technical tracking audit?</summary><p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">No. It is a free self-assessment based on your answers. It does not access or inspect your implementation.</p></details><details class="rounded-xl border border-border bg-background p-5"><summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold">Will the Health Check change my analytics setup?</summary><p class="mt-3 text-muted-foreground">No. It only provides recommendations. Any audit or implementation work is scoped separately.</p></details></div><p class="mt-8 text-center text-muted-foreground">Need implementation evidence rather than a self-assessment? <a class="font-semibold text-primary underline underline-offset-4" href="/services/tracking-audit/">Request a Tracking Audit</a>.</p></div></section>
